# Pairs with TypeOK. A revision counter that can be bumped outside a decision
# write leaves the declared 0..Cardinality(Txns) domain, which is exactly what
# TypeOK is there to notice.
MODULE: TypeOkRevisionRunaway
TARGET: TypeOK
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: bumps the registry revision outside any decision write, so it leaves its declared domain

--- FIND
Next ==
    \/ \E t \in Txns : PrepareTx(t)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a revision bump with no decision behind it. Modelled as a real
\* action rather than by widening TypeOK's domain, because the point is to
\* prove TypeOK notices an out-of-domain variable, not that TypeOK can be
\* edited.
RevisionRunaway ==
    /\ revision' = revision + 1
    /\ UNCHANGED <<phase, vote, decision, terminal, pend, orphanDone>>

Next ==
    \/ RevisionRunaway
    \/ \E t \in Txns : PrepareTx(t)
--- END
